course: dictionary
lesson: 1799
title: Closeness: near, warm and close
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Closeness is a noun, and it has three main meanings. It can mean being near to something in space or time, a strong and warm bond between people, or warm, stuffy air in a room.
explain: Use the context to choose the right meaning. «Friendly teasing, like a nickname you both enjoy, can be a sign of closeness.» The words friendly and enjoy show warmth between two people, so here closeness means a strong, warm friendship.
explain: Check your choice by swapping in a meaning. Being near in space does not fit that sentence, because a nickname is not about distance. The right meaning is the one that still makes sense.
fact: Closeness means being near to something in space or time.
fact: Closeness means a strong, warm friendship or love between people, as in the closeness of a family.
fact: Closeness can also mean that the air in a room is warm and stuffy.
fact: «Friendly teasing, like a nickname you both enjoy, can be a sign of closeness.» Here closeness means a warm friendship.
fact: Closeness is uncountable, so you say the closeness, not closenesses.
exercise: «Friendly teasing, like a nickname you both enjoy, can be a sign of closeness.» What does closeness mean here? | Warm, stuffy air in a room | A sudden loud noise | Being near to something in space | *A strong, warm friendship between people
exercise: The closeness of the family was clear at the birthday party. What does closeness mean? | *A strong, warm bond between family members | Being far apart from each other | Warm, stuffy air in the hall | A loud argument
exercise: Which meaning fits this sentence? «The closeness of the holidays made everyone excited.» | *Being near in time | A strong, warm friendship | A loud noise | Being far away from home
test: «The twins shared a special closeness.» What does closeness mean? | Being near the school gate | *A strong, warm bond | A loud noise | Stuffy, warm air
test: «The closeness of the room made the children sleepy.» What does closeness mean? | *Warm, stuffy air | Cool, fresh air | A strong friendship | Being near in time
exam: Jayden asks, what does closeness mean in «Friendly teasing, like a nickname you both enjoy, can be a sign of closeness.»? | A loud noise | *A strong, warm friendship | Being near to something in space | Stuffy air in a room
